  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 130 PM CDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nFriday Night Through Sunday's Rain Chances: Low level jet looks\nto set up again across Kansas into Nebraska Friday night. An \narea of showers and storms again looks to develop and try to \nadvance east into the area Saturday. Highest rain chances are\nnorth of I-44 during the morning and afternoon hours. Many\nlocations will remain cloudy but dry. A stronger shortwave looks\nto build down into Missouri on Sunday with slightly higher rain\nchances. While there are rain chances this weekend, it currently\ndoes not look like complete washouts or anything very\nimpactful. Mean MU CAPE less than 1000j/kg should keep \nlightning chances low. Latest NBM also has about a 20-40% \nprobability for 0.50inch or rain or more across southeast Kansas\ninto western Missouri. Most locations will see less than \n0.50inch of rainfall. Temps will be seasonable and while the NBM\ndoes have highs in the 80s, if clouds are thicker than these \nmay need to be nudged down some.\n\nHigher Rain Chances Next Week: Ensembles continue to suggest\nthat a stronger system will move into the Rockies and eventually\nour region during the Tuesday-Wednesday time frame next week.\nConfidence is high in the rain chances (currently 50-70%)\nhowever significant structural and timing differences in the \ntrough are still evident (either a progressive/amplified trough\nor a closed off low). Alot of this is likely due to the \nuncertainty of the remnants of Hurricane Polo off the coast of \nMexico. Guidance has this potentially curving northeast into the\nBaja and then getting absorbed into our system. If this does \noccur then it would amplify the amount of moisture available \nwith the system. Latest CPC does indicate the potential for \nheavy rainfall with this system which would be welcome given the\nongoing/worsening drought over a large portion of the area.",
